When you spend too much time on a different level, he might turn
peaceful/hostile. Throw him a meaty corpse, and he'll be back on your
heels.

> A quick question on whistles: What effect does blowing a (magic/tin) 
> whistle have on my pet? I should imagine, it's a tool to attract the 
> pet, however, I have been trying it (for stealing from shops and in 
> other situations) without noticing the desired effect of the pet moving 
> straight towards me.

A tin whistle ("You produce a high whistling sound") "calls" a pet,
meaning if it is nearby, it will move towards you. Not necessarily in a
straight line, and it may well be distracted by other things like
monsters or food. Useful when you want to go down stairs, but not
reliable. A magic whistle ("You produce a strange whistling sound")
teleports your pet near you (next to you?). Can be used to rob shops
(stand in doorway, wait until pet picks something up, move away, blow
whistle), but tripe rations are still way more effective.

